       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day. That is about 5 times the usual maximum for metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (2,000\u20132,550 mg/day for most labeling). A dose that high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Common metformin doses are:\n- **425 mg**, which isn't a standard strength\n- **850 mg** three times daily, for 2,550 mg/day\n- **500 mg** or **1000 mg** twice daily\n\nCan you confirm the intended dose? If you really do want 4250 mg per dose, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
