     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day of metformin is about five times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication where that is therapeutic. It would put the patient at serious risk of metformin-associated lactic acidosis, and normal kidney function doesn't prevent that. Entering it here would also skip the pharmacy verification that would normally catch it.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range**, such as 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or another regimen you choose.\n- **Enter the order as a pending or flagged item** for pharmacist review, if there's a specific reason for the dose that I'm missing. I'd need your go-ahead on the note wording.\n- **Help with a different goal.** If you're trying to reach a particular glycemic target, I can enter add-on agents alongside a maximized metformin dose.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
